## Summary
The Council on Education for Public Health is modifying its standards regarding racial disparity, which has faced criticism from scholars. Additionally, the organization is opting out of federal recognition, signaling major changes in public health accreditation.

## Key Points
- The Council on Education for Public Health is changing language in its standards on racial disparity.
- This change has prompted criticism from scholars.
- The council is walking away from federal recognition.
- These actions represent a significant shift in public health accreditation practices.


